.TH TRUE 1
.SH NAME
true, false \- provide truth values
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B true
.PP
.B false
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B true
does nothing, successfully.
.B false
does nothing, unsuccessfully.
They are typically used in input to the Bourne shell,
.BR sh (1),
such as:
.RS
.nf
while true
do
	command
done
.fi
.RE
.PP
(Note that
.B true
can be done more efficiently simply with the null command `:').
.SH "SEE ALSO"
sh(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B true
has exit status zero,
.B false
nonzero.
.sp
